// Copy to Config.xcconfig (git-ignored) and fill in your own project's values.
//
//   Project Settings > API in the Supabase dashboard:
//     Project URL      -> SUPABASE_URL
//     anon public key  -> SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
//
// The anon key is meant to ship inside the app: it grants nothing on its own,
// because every table is behind Row Level Security. The service_role key is
// the opposite -- it bypasses RLS entirely -- and must never appear here, in
// the repository, in CI logs, or in a message to anyone.
//
// Left empty, the app falls back to demo data rather than showing a sign-in
// form with nothing behind it. That is the intended state until a project
// exists.
//
// A URL here needs the // escaped: Xcode treats // as a comment even inside a
// value, so https://x.supabase.co would become "https:". Hence the indirection
// below -- uncomment both lines and fill in the ref.
// SUPABASE_SLASHES = $()/$()/
// SUPABASE_URL = https:$(SUPABASE_SLASHES)your-project-ref.supabase.co
// SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = your-anon-public-key

SUPABASE_URL =
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY =
